# vyatta-rest
provides the vyatta rest interface

## Legacy session storage

The REST startup script creates `/var/run/gui` as root with mode `0700`.
The FastCGI reader and the Perl `SessionKey.pm` issuer use root-owned regular
files with mode `0600` and one hard link. The lock file remains in place
between operations. Valid sessions in a store that meets these requirements
keep their existing header and cookie formats. Newly issued session IDs use
16 hexadecimal characters drawn from eight random bytes.

On an upgrade from the former shared runtime directory, reboot to create
fresh runtime state. Startup refuses an existing directory with unsafe
ownership or permissions. Sessions stored in that directory must be issued
again. The Perl issuer now requires an already privileged caller. A legacy
issuer running as an ordinary web-server account cannot use the session store.
